      "sIndex": 1,
      "id": "P3-S1",
      "pIndex": 3
    },
    "text": "Last year, the Transportation Security Administration (TSA) found in a secret check that undercover investigators were able to sneak weapons—both fake and real—past airport security nearly every time they tried.",
    "translation": "去年，美国运输安全管理局（TSA）在一次秘密检查中发现，卧底调查员能够携带武器（不管真假）成功通过机场安检，几乎屡试不爽。",
    "syntaxAnalysis": {
      "structureType": "复合句（含宾语从句与时间状语从句）",
      "mainClause": "the TSA found in a secret check that undercover investigators were able to sneak weapons... past airport security...",
      "modifiers": "Last year 为时间状语；in a secret check 为方式状语；that 引导 found 的宾语从句；破折号 both fake and real 作 weapons 的同位插入语；nearly every time (that) they tried 为省略关系代词的时间状语从句。",
      "corePattern": "sneak sth. past sb./sth.（将……偷偷带过/溜过）。"
    },
    "rawFields": {
      "isTopicSentence": false,
      "isKeyEvidence": false,
      "isUnderlined": false,
      "underlinedPhrases": []
